DESIGN ATTRIBUTION
==================

One third-party library is vendored, under identicon/reference/vendor/, and it
is named in full below. Everything else here credits design inspiration only,
with the licence status of each source stated plainly.

This file previously said that nothing was vendored, on the grounds that "the
offline scope removed every reason to". That stopped being true when the
identicon acquired an external conformance reference: without the library in
the tree, identicon/vectors.json is a file this repository merely asserts is
reference output, and nobody can check it. Vendoring is what makes the
assertion falsifiable. The vendored copy is a *test fixture* -- it is never
imported by the evaluator, the plasmoid or the CLI, and it ships in nothing.

