stewartlord/identicon.js  -- VENDORED
  BSD-2-Clause licensed. Copyright (c) 2018, Stewart Lord.
  Vendored at identicon/reference/vendor/, unmodified, from upstream commit
  7063ae16142fd39d3563699b9af2dc321326ff52 (2022-03-24). The full licence text
  is retained verbatim at identicon/reference/vendor/LICENSE, as BSD-2-Clause
  requires for redistribution in source form; its copyright notice, conditions
  list and disclaimer are reproduced there in full and must stay with the files.

  It is the normative reference for the project identicon. It generates
  identicon/vectors.json, and tests/test_conformance.py re-runs it on every
  test run to confirm the pinned vectors are still what it produces. Its grid
  and colour rules were transliterated into Python in
  identicon/claude-state-identicon.py; no code was copied into that file.

  Vendored rather than fetched because a downloaded reference can vanish -- one
  did, during the week this was written -- and a conformance file nobody can
  re-derive is indistinguishable from a file we made up.

dgraham/identicon
  MIT licensed.
  Evaluated, not used. Its grid rule was transcribed from src/lib.rs and
  src/nibbler.rs and confirmed to agree with the reference on all ten vectors,
  which is the evidence that the grid is a property of the convention rather
  than of one author. Its colour rule differs and was not taken. No code copied,
  nothing vendored, and it is not required to build or test this project.

